    placement: at least 1 cell from grid edge; typically 2+ cells interior
    sides_with_objects: 0-4 cardinal sides may have an adjacent object (0 = decorative)
  moving_objects:
    count: 3-7 per grid, each a 4-connected monochromatic component
    colors: each object has a unique color, not 7 (bg) or 9 (maroon)
    size: 1-19 pixels; majority 1-5 [observed]
    shape: arbitrary 4-connected polyomino
    maroon_contact: each object is 4-adjacent to exactly one maroon component on exactly one cardinal side
    adjacency_width: typically 1-2 maroon cells touched per object
  push_rule: each object translates away from its maroon contact side until its leading edge hits the grid boundary
  push_distance: 0-8 cells; median ~3; dist>=1 for 95% of objects
  no_collision: moved objects must not overlap each other or maroon in output
  swept_path: object movement from input to output is unobstructed; every intermediate translated position crosses only background outside the object's own cells [observed]
  output: same grid with objects at pushed positions; maroon unchanged; original positions cleared to bg

generation_strategy:
